---
title: Jordan Marsh's Blueberry Muffins
description: Sugar-topped blueberry muffins from the old Boston department store, with some berries crushed into the batter.
tags: [muffins, baking]
course: breakfast
source:
  name: NYT Cooking
  author: Marian Burros
  url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/2868-jordan-marshs-blueberry-muffins
yield: 12%muffins
time: 1h10m
---

Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C).

Cream the @softened butter{1/2%cup} and @sugar{248%g} (1 1/4 cups) until light.

Add the @eggs{2}, one at a time, beating well after each addition. Add the @vanilla extract{1%tsp}.

Sift together the @flour{240%g}(2 cups), @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @baking powder{2%tsp}, and add to the creamed mixture alternately with the @milk{1/2%cup}.

Crush 1/2 cup of the @blueberries{2%cup}(washed, drained and picked over) with a #fork{}, and mix into the batter. Fold in the remaining whole berries.

Line a 12-cup standard #muffin tin{} with #cupcake liners{}, and fill with batter. Sprinkle the remaining @&sugar{12%g} (3 tsp) over the tops of the muffins, and bake at 375°F (190°C) for about ~bake{30-35%minutes}.

Remove the muffins from the tin and cool at least ~cool{30%minutes}. Store uncovered, or the muffins will be too moist the second day, if they last that long.
